module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.SymmetricAlgebraAffineSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.NormalCone.SymmetricQuotient
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.QuasiRegularCharts
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Sequence.QuasiRegular.GradedBasis
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Condition (3) of Tag 063M out of quasi-regularity: `Sym*(C_{Z/X}) ≅ C_{Z/X,*}`

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a quasi-regular immersion.  This file proves that the canonical map of
[Stacks, Tag 0632]

`Stacks.Conormal.conormalSymmetricHom i : Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}`

is an isomorphism in **every** degree.  This is condition (3) of the right-hand side of
[Stacks, Tag 063M], in the direction out of quasi-regularity; conditions (1) and (2) in that
direction are
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isQuasiRegularImmersion`
and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf`
`.isFiniteLocallyFree_conormalSheaf_of_isQuasiRegularImmersion`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Conormal.surjective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart`: over an affine closed-immersion
  chart the canonical map is surjective on sections, for any immersion.
* `Stacks.Conormal.injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart`: **over a quasi-regular affine
  chart it is injective on sections.**
* `Stacks.Conormal.injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app` and
  `Stacks.Conormal.mono_conormalSymmetricHom_app`: for a quasi-regular immersion it is injective
  on the sections over *every* open, hence a monomorphism.
* `Stacks.Conormal.isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app`: **[Stacks, Tag 063M] condition (3) out of
  quasi-regularity** — for a quasi-regular immersion the canonical map is an isomorphism in
  every degree.
* `Stacks.Conormal.chartSymPowEquiv`: over an affine closed-immersion chart the sections of
  `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` are `Symⁿ` of the sections of `𝒞_{Z/X}`.
* `Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegular_chart_of_isIso`: **the chart-level converse** — if the
  canonical map is an isomorphism in every degree, then over an affine closed-immersion chart
  whose chart ideal is generated by as many functions as the conormal sheaf has free generators
  there, the generating sequence is quasi-regular.

## Implementation notes

**The chart computation is a rank count, not an identification of the map.**  Over a chart `U`
of `X` whose chart ideal `I` is generated by a quasi-regular sequence `f₀, …, f_{c-1}`, the
degree-`n` sections of the target are `Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`, which
`Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular.GradedPresentation.basis` makes free over `Γ(Z, i⁻¹U)` on
the monomials of degree `n` in `c` variables — that statement rests on
`Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular.symPowEquivTcomp`, the affine shadow of Tag 0632 for a
quasi-regular sequence.  The degree-one case makes `𝒞_{Z/X}(i⁻¹U)` free on the `c` classes of
the generators, so the sections of `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` over the chart — which are `Symⁿ` of the
sections, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraPieceEquiv`, the chart being
affine — are free on the *same* index set.  A surjection onto a finite module from a module
admitting an injection into it is injective (`OrzechProperty.injective_of_surjective_of_injective`,
available over any commutative ring), and the canonical map is surjective on chart sections by
`Stacks.Conormal.exists_conormalSymmetricHom_app_eq_localMap`.  So the map is *not* compared
with the algebraic comparison map on monomials; only the two free modules are compared, and
they are compared through their index sets.

**Injectivity has to be proved over every open.**  There is no "locally injective implies
monomorphism" lemma for `SheafOfModules` in this library —
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EpiLocallySurjective` has only the epimorphism
half, and Mathlib's version is stated for a concretely-valued sheaf category.
So the chart statement is propagated by hand: the quasi-regular affine charts are a basis of
opens of `Z` by `Stacks.Conormal.exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_mem`, a section killed by the
map restricts to zero on each of them, and `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` is a sheaf.  This is the same route
degree zero takes in `Stacks.Conormal.isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app_zero`.

**Why not a rank comparison of sheaves.**
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_iff_epi_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank`
(Tag 089Q) would deduce the isomorphism from surjectivity, but it needs both sides to be
finite locally free of one and the same *constant* rank, which a quasi-regular immersion of
varying codimension does not provide.

**How this file feeds Tag 063M.**  The converse direction is here only chart by chart, as
`Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegular_chart_of_isIso`, whose algebraic half is
`Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular.isQuasiRegular_of_basisTcomp`.  What that leaves is Tag 063M's
*shrinking* step: producing, around each point of `Z` out of conditions (1) and (2), an affine
closed-immersion chart whose chart ideal `I` is generated by exactly as many functions as the
rank of `𝒞_{Z/X}` there.  That step, and with it the `iff` of Tag 063M, is
`Stacks.Conormal.exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_of_isFiniteLocallyFree` and
`Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegularImmersion_iff` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.ConormalQuasiRegularCriterion`, which is where
the tag is registered for the whole statement; the attribute in this file stays scoped to the
clause it carries.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.5 (Tag 063M)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063M)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.2 (Tag 0632)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0632)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.2 (Tag 063G)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 061P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/061P)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular

universe u

namespace Stacks.Conormal

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### The pieces as `𝒪_Z`-modules -/

/-- The degree-`k` piece of the conormal algebra, read as an `𝒪_Z`-module.  The spelling matters:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def`, so the instance `Module Γ(Z, V) Γ(ℳ, V)` on
sections is found only at this spelling. -/
abbrev conormalPiece (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (k : ℤ) : Z.Modules :=
  (conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece k

/-- The degree-`k` piece of `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X})`, read as an `𝒪_Z`-module. -/
abbrev conormalSymPiece (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (k : ℤ) : Z.Modules :=
  (conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece k

/-! ### The chart preimage is affine -/

/-- The preimage of an affine open over which an immersion restricts to a closed immersion is
affine: it is the preimage of an affine open of the coborder of the range under the closed
factor. -/
theorem isAffineOpen_preimage_affineChart (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) :
    IsAffineOpen (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
  coborderAffineChart_preimage i U hU ▸
    ((coborderAffineChart i U hU).2.preimage i.liftCoborder)

/-! ### Surjectivity on chart sections -/

/-- **Over an affine closed-immersion chart the canonical map is surjective on sections.**  Every
degree-`n` section of the conormal algebra over the chart is the class of a section of the
`n`-th power of the chart ideal, and such a class is hit by
`Stacks.Conormal.exists_conormalSymmetricHom_app_eq_localMap`. -/
@[ega "0 19.5.2" "more general"]
theorem surjective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (conormalAlgebra i).localMap_surjective U hU n x
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_conormalSymmetricHom_app_eq_localMap i U hU n a
  exact ⟨s, hs.trans ha⟩

/-! ### The chart presentation of a graded piece -/

/-- **The local associated-graded presentation of the conormal algebra over an affine
closed-immersion chart whose chart ideal carries a chosen finite generating sequence**, read as
a presentation of the degree-`n` piece of the associated graded ring of that ideal.  The data
is the six laws of
`Stacks.Conormal.ConormalAlgebraData` together with surjectivity of the map on functions over
the chart. -/
def chartPresentation (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) {c : ℕ} (f : Fin c → Γ(X, U.1))
    (hspan : chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (n : ℕ) :
    GradedPresentation Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) c n
      Γ(conormalPiece i (n : ℤ), i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) where
  f := f
  ψ := (i.app U.1).hom
  surjective_ψ := AlgebraicGeometry.app_surjective_of_closedRestriction i U hU
  J := chartIdeal i U
  span_J := hspan
  ker_ψ := rfl
  g := (conormalAlgebra i).localMap U hU n
  smul_g r x := (conormalAlgebra i).localMap_smul U hU n r x (r • x) (by
    rw [SetLike.val_smul, smul_eq_mul])
  surjective_g := (conormalAlgebra i).localMap_surjective U hU n
  ker_g x := (conormalAlgebra i).localMap_eq_zero_iff U hU n x

/-! ### The sections of `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` over a chart -/

/-- **Over an affine closed-immersion chart the sections of `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` are `Symⁿ` of the
sections of `𝒞_{Z/X}`.**  The chart preimage is affine and `𝒞_{Z/X}` is quasi-coherent, so the
sheafification unit is bijective there by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.bijective_symmetricAlgebra_sheafifyUnit_of_isAffineOpen`. -/
def chartSymPowEquiv (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) (n : ℕ) :
    SymPow.symmetricPower n Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
      ≃ₗ[Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)] Γ(conormalSymPiece i (n : ℤ), i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
  haveI hVaff : IsAffineOpen (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := isAffineOpen_preimage_affineChart i U hU
  haveI hqc : (conormalPiece i 1).IsQuasicoherent := (conormalAlgebra i).isQuasicoherent 1
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (R := Z.ringCatSheaf)
      (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj) (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalPiece i 1).val))
      (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))).hom
    (Scheme.Modules.bijective_symmetricAlgebra_sheafifyUnit_of_isAffineOpen
      (conormalPiece i 1) hVaff (n : ℤ))

/-! ### Injectivity on the sections over a quasi-regular chart -/

/-- **Over a quasi-regular affine chart the canonical map is injective on sections.**  Both sides
are free `Γ(Z, i⁻¹U)`-modules on the monomials of degree `n` in the `c` generators of the chart
ideal: the target by `Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular.GradedPresentation.basis`, the source
because the chart is affine, so its sections are `Symⁿ` of the sections of `𝒞_{Z/X}`, which are
free on the `c` classes of the generators.  The map is surjective, hence injective, because a
surjection onto a finite module which admits an injection from its own source is injective. -/
@[ega "IV 16.9.3" "(ii)"]
theorem injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl))
    {c : ℕ} (f : Fin c → Γ(X, U.1))
    (hspan : chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (hqr : RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular Γ(X, U.1) (List.ofFn f)) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Injective (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) := by
  have b1 : Module.Basis (Fin c) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
    GradedPresentation.basisOne (chartPresentation i U hU f hspan 1) hqr
  have : Module.Finite Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
    Module.Finite.of_basis b1
  let L := chartSymPowEquiv i U hU n
  let Θ : Γ(conormalSymPiece i (n : ℤ), i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)]
      Γ(conormalPiece i (n : ℤ), i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
    ((SymPow.basisSymmetricPower b1 n).map L).equiv
      ((chartPresentation i U hU f hspan n).basis hqr) (Equiv.refl _)
  have : Module.Finite Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalSymPiece i (n : ℤ), i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
    Module.Finite.equiv L
  have : Module.Finite Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i (n : ℤ), i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
    Module.Finite.equiv Θ
  exact OrzechProperty.injective_of_surjective_of_injective Θ.toLinearMap
    (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val
      (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))).hom Θ.injective
    (surjective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart i U hU n)

/-! ### Injectivity over every open -/

/-- **For a quasi-regular immersion the canonical map is injective on the sections over every
open.**  The quasi-regular affine charts are a basis of opens of `Z`, a section killed by the map
restricts to zero on each of them by
`Stacks.Conormal.injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart`, and `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` is a sheaf. -/
theorem injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (h : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsQuasiRegularImmersion i) (n : ℕ)
    (V : Z.Opens) :
    Function.Injective (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op V)) := by
  have hzero : ∀ t : ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op V),
      PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op V) t = 0 →
        t = 0 := by
    intro t ht
    refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext
      ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).isSheaf (U := op V) ?_
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨U, hUclosed, hxU, hUV, c, f, hspan, hqr⟩ :=
      exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_mem i h V x hx
    refine ⟨i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1, hUV, hxU, ?_⟩
    have hconv : ∀ s : ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op V),
        ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op s =
          ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hUV).op s :=
      fun _ => rfl
    have key : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
          (((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hUV).op t) = 0 :=
      (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val
          (homOfLE hUV).op t).trans
        ((congrArg (((conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hUV).op)
          ht).trans (map_zero _))
    rw [hconv, hconv, map_zero]
    exact injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_chart i U hUclosed f hspan hqr n
      (key.trans (map_zero _).symm)
  intro y y' hyy'
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (hzero (y - y') (by rw [map_sub, hyy', sub_self]))

/-- **For a quasi-regular immersion the canonical map is a monomorphism in every nonnegative
degree.**  Monomorphy of a morphism of sheaves of modules is injectivity on the sections over
every open, which is `Stacks.Conormal.injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app`. -/
theorem mono_conormalSymmetricHom_app (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (h : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsQuasiRegularImmersion i) (n : ℕ) :
    Mono ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)) :=
  (SheafOfModules.forget Z.ringCatSheaf).mono_of_mono_map
    (PresheafOfModules.mono_of_injective (f := ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val)
      fun V => injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app i h n V.unop)

/-! ### Condition (3) of Tag 063M -/

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 063M], condition (3) in the direction out of quasi-regularity.**  For a
quasi-regular immersion the canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` of [Stacks, Tag 0632] is
an isomorphism in **every** degree.  In a negative degree both sides vanish.  In a nonnegative
degree it is an epimorphism by `Stacks.Conormal.epi_conormalSymmetricHom_app`, which holds for
any immersion, and a monomorphism by `Stacks.Conormal.mono_conormalSymmetricHom_app`, which is
where quasi-regularity enters: over a quasi-regular affine chart both sides are free on the
monomials of the degree in the generators of the chart ideal. -/
theorem isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (h : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsQuasiRegularImmersion i) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app n) := by
  rcases lt_or_ge n 0 with hn | hn
  · have h1 : Limits.IsZero ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece n) :=
      Scheme.Modules.isZero_symmetricAlgebra_piece Z ((conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece 1) n hn
    exact ⟨⟨0, h1.eq_of_src _ _, ((conormalAlgebra i).negative_isZero n hn).eq_of_src _ _⟩⟩
  · obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Int.eq_ofNat_of_zero_le hn
    have := mono_conormalSymmetricHom_app i h m
    have := epi_conormalSymmetricHom_app i (m : ℤ)
    exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-! ### Towards the converse -/

/-- An isomorphism `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X}) ≅ 𝒞_{Z/X,n}` read on the sections over an open: an
isomorphism of sheaves of modules evaluates to an isomorphism of modules of sections, hence to
a bijection. -/
def pieceEquivOfIsIso (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (n : ℕ)
    (h : IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ))) (V : Z.Opens) :
    Γ(conormalSymPiece i (n : ℤ), V) ≃ₗ[Γ(Z, V)] Γ(conormalPiece i (n : ℤ), V) :=
  haveI := h
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op V)).hom
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
      ((SheafOfModules.forget Z.ringCatSheaf ⋙
          PresheafOfModules.evaluation Z.ringCatSheaf.obj (op V)).map
        ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ))))

/-- **The chart-level converse of condition (3).**  Let `U` be an affine open of `X` over which
`i` restricts to a closed immersion and whose chart ideal is generated by `c` functions `f`, and
suppose the conormal sheaf has `c` free generators over the chart.  If the canonical map of
[Stacks, Tag 0632] is an isomorphism in every degree then `f` is a quasi-regular sequence.

Over the chart the sections of `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` are `Symⁿ` of the sections of `𝒞_{Z/X}`
(`Stacks.Conormal.chartSymPowEquiv`), hence free on the monomials of degree `n` in `c`
variables; the isomorphism carries that basis to a basis of `Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹` over `Γ(Z, i⁻¹U)`, which
`Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular.GradedPresentation.basisTcompOfBasis` reads as a basis over
`Γ(X, U)/I`; and a sequence whose graded pieces are free on the monomials of their degree is
quasi-regular by `Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular.isQuasiRegular_of_basisTcomp`.

This is the whole of the converse direction of [Stacks, Tag 063M] except for its shrinking
step — producing, around each point and out of conditions (1) and (2), an affine
closed-immersion chart on which the chart ideal is generated by as many functions as the rank
of the conormal sheaf there — which is
`Stacks.Conormal.exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_of_isFiniteLocallyFree`. -/
@[ega "IV 16.9.3" "(i), special case"]
theorem isQuasiRegular_chart_of_isIso (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) {c : ℕ} (f : Fin c → Γ(X, U.1))
    (hspan : chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (b1 : Module.Basis (Fin c) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
    (hiso : ∀ n : ℤ, IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app n)) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular Γ(X, U.1) (List.ofFn f) :=
  isQuasiRegular_of_basisTcomp f fun n =>
    (chartPresentation i U hU f hspan n).basisTcompOfBasis
      (((SymPow.basisSymmetricPower b1 n).map (chartSymPowEquiv i U hU n)).map
        (pieceEquivOfIsIso i n (hiso (n : ℤ)) (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))

end Stacks.Conormal

end
